fingerprint: qbt2000: return success for repeated IPC/WUHB toggles

The Samsung biometrics HAL sends QBT2000_ENABLE_IPC, QBT2000_DISABLE_IPC,
QBT2000_ENABLE_WUHB and QBT2000_DISABLE_WUHB even when the interrupt is
already in the requested state. The driver correctly skips the second
enable_irq()/disable_irq(), but returned -EINVAL. QFPControl_DeviceEnableInt()
treats that as fatal, so enrollment aborts halfway ("Something went wrong").

This is the source form of the device-tested binary patch made by
patch_fingerprint.py for 5.10.260-g0d060df61c11-dirty. In that module the
patched instruction (.text+0x1dd4 in qbt2000_ioctl, mov w20, #-0x16) is the
shared rc = -EINVAL tail reached only by these four "already ..." paths. The
guard and its log message are unchanged; only the return value becomes 0.

Applied by .github/workflows/build.yml before compiling; the build fails if
it no longer applies to the kernel source.

diff --git a/drivers/fingerprint/qbt2000_common.c b/drivers/fingerprint/qbt2000_common.c
index f888924..0e14964 100644
--- a/drivers/fingerprint/qbt2000_common.c
+++ b/drivers/fingerprint/qbt2000_common.c
@@ -306,7 +306,6 @@ static int qbt2000_enable_ipc(struct qbt2000_drvdata *drvdata)
 
 	if (drvdata->fw_ipc.gpio) {
 		if (drvdata->enabled_ipc) {
-			rc = -EINVAL;
 			pr_err("already enabled ipc\n");
 		} else {
 			enable_irq(drvdata->fw_ipc.irq);
@@ -327,7 +326,6 @@ static int qbt2000_disable_ipc(struct qbt2000_drvdata *drvdata)
 			disable_irq(drvdata->fw_ipc.irq);
 			drvdata->enabled_ipc = false;
 		} else {
-			rc = -EINVAL;
 			pr_err("already disabled ipc\n");
 		}
 	}
@@ -341,7 +339,6 @@ static int qbt2000_enable_wuhb(struct qbt2000_drvdata *drvdata)
 
 	if (drvdata->fd_gpio.gpio) {
 		if (drvdata->enabled_wuhb) {
-			rc = -EINVAL;
 			pr_err("already enabled wuhb\n");
 		} else {
 			enable_irq(drvdata->fd_gpio.irq);
@@ -373,7 +370,6 @@ static int qbt2000_disable_wuhb(struct qbt2000_drvdata *drvdata)
 			disable_irq_wake(drvdata->fd_gpio.irq);
 			drvdata->enabled_wuhb = false;
 		} else {
-			rc = -EINVAL;
 			pr_err("already disabled wuhb\n");
 		}
 	}
